  "inherited_parent_limits": [
    "Original QVF architecture retains 64 global classical code entries and the audited 5q circuit/readout.",
    "The benchmarking recipe includes RGB-plus-edge training, constant learning rate and common positional frequencies. It is not the paper training recipe.",
    "Spatial code budgets are 336 at32px and21504 at256px; vanilla64 is not a storage-matched ablation.",
    "Positional frequencies are six at32px and nine at256px, common to all methods within each panel.",
    "Methods share update/coordinate/loss budgets within a panel, not equal parameters, gates, total shots or time.",
    "The two panels use different datasets; their scores do not form a resolution-only ablation.",
    "Z6/Z7 Stanford test scores have already been inspected. This is benchmark reuse, not a new confirmatory holdout.",
    "New-image codes are fitted with a frozen decoder; no encoder, VAE or diffusion.",
    "No hardware execution, quantum advantage or convergence claim.",
    "New arms use the same seven-qubit spatial circuits, encoding stages and measurement map as their corresponding Z6/Z7 references.",
    "Attention is classical, within a fixed 5x5-token window around each of five spatial slots at each scale. It is not global attention.",
    "The prior five-qubit attention reference uses dense attention, amplitude encoding and a different circuit. That contrast does not isolate circuit count.",
    "Mean and output-attention arms execute three independent seven-qubit circuits; coherent fusion uses one nine-qubit multiplexed register, not a 21-qubit state.",
    "Output attention is a 16-parameter classical softmax over measured outputs. Coherent fusion uses the existing quantum routing operations.",
    "Attention adds classical parameters and work; circuit and shot budgets differ between fusion strategies.",
    "Z8 and earlier benchmark results were inspected before this extension; this is not an untouched confirmatory test set."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "This arm changes the original QVF global code from64 to256 entries and widens the first MLP input accordingly. All hidden widths, quantum gates and RGB readout are unchanged.",
    "At width128 the larger input adds24576 shared classical weights. This is not a fixed-parameter or equal-compute comparison.",
    "The original initializer is retained. Different input widths change random-number consumption and fan-in; pairing seed labels does not imply identical circuit/hidden-layer initial tensors.",
    "The per-coordinate code initialization standard deviation and the panel L2-norm penalty coefficient are unchanged. Code norms can grow with dimension.",
    "A256-value code still does not match336 spatial entries at32px or21504 at256px. This control tests a larger global code, not the full capacity-versus-locality attribution.",
    "All new runs start fresh. Prior test results were inspected, so this is a benchmark extension, not an untouched confirmatory test set."
  ],
